      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If authorities discover undisclosed assets, the penalties are often far more severe than just the unpaid tax and interest. You can expect to face significant financial penalties, which are often calculated as a percentage of the tax that should have been paid, and this can be quite substantial. Furthermore, deliberate concealment can lead to criminal investigations, which is a much more serious matter than a simple administrative error. It's a situation where the tax authority views the action as a deliberate attempt to evade their requirements.",
      "source": "target",
